From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:46:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panda: before_loadvm hook before qemu_loadvm_state loads RAM

The RAM a load writes isn't logged dirty, and a load that fails partway
(an unknown device section after the RAM section, for instance) leaves RAM
half written. Tell PANDA before the load starts, success or not, for
loadvm, panda_revert, an rr start and an incoming migration alike: an
in-memory snapshot that copies back only dirty pages must copy all RAM
on its next restore. (after_loadvm runs only after a successful
load_snapshot.)

SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
Origin: new
---
 migration/savevm.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/migration/savevm.c b/migration/savevm.c
index 91edbe2315f9330a1ec5f63b6f8841721f561459..d898b10a06a3b3c7515f128c93242f133a0f4b08 100644
--- a/migration/savevm.c
+++ b/migration/savevm.c
@@ -3110,6 +3110,8 @@ int qemu_loadvm_state(QEMUFile *f, Error **errp)
 
     cpu_synchronize_all_pre_loadvm();
 
+    /* RAM is about to change without dirty bits, whether or not the load succeeds */
+    panda_before_loadvm();
     ret = qemu_loadvm_state_main(f, mis, errp);
     qemu_event_set(&mis->main_thread_load_event);
 
